From 926848b165042c7c77b80f1573afed3d8ec5e0e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoXider <neoxider@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:18:10 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] cq: lossless f16e3 KV type (3-bit exponent windows +
 escapes, overflow pool), half-math GQA decode for all KV types, pooled f16
 scratch

- GGML_TYPE_F16E3 = 61: 128-value superblock in 244 bytes (0.953 of F16); superblocks with more than 8 escapes go raw to
  a device pool (env CQ_F16E3_POOL_MIB, default 256); exact for every F16 bit pattern
- fattn-vec-gqa: K/V of every type (f16, f16d4, f16e3, q8_0, q4_0) decoded to half, f16 dot products (no q8_1 Q)
- CQ_FA_SCRATCH_POOL=1: f16 copies of quantized K/V for prefill come from the lazily growing CUDA pool instead of the
  worst-case compute buffer
- CQ_VRAM_REPORT also prints the f16e3 pool usage
